{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/2810","id":2934785426,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz886u7UWS","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2810","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2810.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2810.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2810","number":2810,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[Fix] Headscale API Bypasses Middleware","user":{"login":"ElyasAsmad","id":78308067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MzA4MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78308067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElyasAsmad","html_url":"https://github.com/ElyasAsmad","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElyasAsmad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElyasAsmad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElyasAsmad/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElyasAsmad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElyasAsmad/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElyasAsmad/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElyasAsmad/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElyasAsmad/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElyasAsmad/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# Description\r\nThis PR aims to fix #2809 \r\n\r\n# General Overview\r\nThe previous implementation checks if `err` is not null and returned from the `writer.Write` function call. In majority cases, the `Write` function call will be triggered successfully without any error. In an unauthorized scenario (where the API caller does not provide API key), Headscale already know the API caller is unauthorized but since the guard `return` statement is ONLY called if `writer.Write` returns an error, thus the middleware will continue executing.\r\n\